mitted says nothing about commits."},{"criterion":"5. No fake progress percentage and no invented 'N of M criteria' indicator","status":"met","detail":"Neither exists in the card. Two checks keep it that way: test-ustabasi.mjs:352-363 greps the Tile+Wall region of the source for percent/progress/toFixed/*100 and for done_criteria|findings, and test-wall-ui.mjs:207 greps the browser's rendered innerText for any digit followed by %."},{"criterion":"6. Card text short and human, no report-speak","status":"met","detail":"The card body is the last event's first line (with the log's [user] tag stripped and `start` events replaced by the ticket's goal, since that line was 'worker round 1 pid 74155 model … account …'), then 'open 15h 18m', then 'worker r2 · 49m in this round · 3 commits · 2 notes', then 'last <subject>'. test-wall-ui.mjs:203-204 asserts no pid and no model name reach the screen. Judged by reading; not mechanically testable beyond that."},{"criterion":"7. Readable on a phone in portrait: one column, no horizontal scroll","status":"met","detail":"The grid is `repeat(auto-fill, minmax(min(100%, 340px), 1fr))` with minWidth: 0 on every box and nowrap+ellipsis on the title, project heading and commit subject (Ustabasi.tsx:183-202). web/scripts/test-wall-ui.mjs drives a real headless Chrome at 390x844 and 320x568 and asserts each column takes the full width, documentElement.scrollWidth === clientWidth, and that no element's right edge passes innerWidth — including a deliberately unbreakable 200-char commit subject in the fixture. I read the assertions; the passing exit status is the worker's report, and this suite is deliberately out of CI because it needs a browser."},{"criterion":"8. Existing typecheck/test commands green, commands named in the report","status":"met","detail":"The report names them: the 11 daemon scripts (test_ustabasi now added to the CI loop, .github/workflows/ci.yml:50), `npm run build` (tsc --noEmit && vite build), `npm test`, `npm run test